        "original_id": "af2d4164-a84e-555c-b4e3-0037765f6284",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness; Charles Edward Stuart; Henry Benedict Stuart; James Francis Edward Stuart; Ignazio Busca\n- Events: Jacobite rising of 1745; Battle of Culloden\n- Roles: Perthshire gentleman; titular archbishop of Emesa\n- Places: Great Britain; Frascati\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Edward Stuart led the unsuccessful Jacobite rising of 1745 in an effort to restore his family to the throne of Great Britain.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was a Perthshire gentleman who joined Charles Edward Stuart's 1745 rebellion.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was captured at the Battle of Culloden and was later convicted of treason.\n- Henry Benedict Stuart, unlike his father James Francis Edward Stuart and his brother Charles Edward Stuart, made no effort to seize the throne.\n- Ignazio Busca was elected titular archbishop of Emesa and was consecrated in Frascati on September 17, 1775, by Henry Benedict Stuart.",
